    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1016/j.jfineco.2026.104311",
      "sequence": 3,
      "source_sequence": 3,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "Firm-to-firm financial linkages and dollar risk transmission",
      "title_cn": "企业间的金融联系和美元风险传递",
      "authors": [
        "Bryan Hardy",
        "Felipe Saffie",
        "Ina Simonovska"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "We study how U.S. dollar fluctuations transmit through domestic supply chains in emerging markets. Large firms borrow in foreign currency and extend trade credit to domestic partners, exposing the supply chain to exchange rate risk. We develop a model where financially constrained suppliers pass through shocks to buyers, while unconstrained firms absorb them. Using quarterly firm-level data from 19 emerging markets, we provide empirical evidence consistent with the model’s predictions. We find that even highly exposed firms reduce trade credit only modestly following a depreciation, while accepting large profit losses, suggesting that firm-to-firm credit relationships partially shield downstream firms from financial shocks.",
      "abstract_cn": "我们研究美元波动如何通过新兴市场的国内供应链传导。大公司借入外币并向国内合作伙伴提供贸易信贷，使供应链面临汇率风险。我们开发了一个模型，在该模型中，财务受限的供应商将冲击传递给买家，而不受约束的公司则吸收冲击。使用来自19新兴市场的季度公司级数据，我们提供了与模型预测一致的经验证据。我们发现，即使是风险敞口较高的企业，在贬值后也只会小幅减少贸易信贷，同时接受巨额利润损失，这表明企业与企业之间的信贷关系在一定程度上保护了下游企业免受金融冲击。",
      "abstract_snippet_en": "",
      "doi": "10.1016/j.jfineco.2026.104311",
