    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1016/j.jfineco.2026.104326",
      "sequence": 9,
      "source_sequence": 9,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "Changing the board game: Horizontal spillovers of gender quotas",
      "title_cn": "改变棋盘游戏：性别配额的横向溢出",
      "authors": [
        "Luigi Guiso",
        "Fabiano Schivardi",
        "Luana Zaccaria"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "We examine the effects of mandatory board gender quotas on unregulated firms that are connected to regulated ones via interlocking directorates. After the introduction of quotas, connected firms significantly increase their share of female directors relative to similar unconnected firms. The spillover effects are substantial — at least as large as the direct effects on regulated firms, challenging previous claims that quotas have no broader impact on women in business. Our results suggest that quotas indirectly broaden the supply of candidates for connected firms, along dimensions that include, but are not limited to, gender.",
      "abstract_cn": "我们研究了强制性董事会性别配额对通过连锁董事会与受监管公司相连的不受监管公司的影响。引入配额后，与类似的非关联公司相比，关联公司的女性董事比例显着增加。溢出效应是巨大的——至少与对受监管企业的直接影响一样大，这挑战了之前关于配额对商界女性没有更广泛影响的说法。我们的结果表明，配额间接扩大了关联公司的候选人供应，包括但不限于性别。",
      "abstract_snippet_en": "",
      "doi": "10.1016/j.jfineco.2026.104326",
